<span class="ltx_personname">Shane Bergsma
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>Cerebras Systems
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email: </span><a href="mailto:"><span id="id2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">shane.bergsma@cerebras.net</span></a>
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Avraham Sheinin
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>Cerebras Systems
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Natalia Vassilieva
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>Cerebras Systems
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Shaheer Muhammad
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>Cerebras Systems
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Preslav Nakov
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>MBZUAI, Abu Dhabi
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>Abu Dhabi, UAE
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Gurpreet Gosal
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>Cerebras Systems
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email: </span><a href="mailto:"><span id="id3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gurpreet.gosal@cerebras.net</span></a>
</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">Continual pre-training (CPT) for domain adaptation must balance target-domain gains with stability on the base domain. Existing CPT scaling laws typically assume a fixed pre-training budget, which limits their ability to forecast adaptation outcomes for models trained at different tokens-per-parameter (PTPP). We present <em id="abstract1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">PTPP-aware</em> adaptation scaling laws that make the pre-training budget an explicit variable, enabling accurate <em id="abstract1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">prediction</em> of adaptation loss at unseen <math id="abstract1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>. On a multilingual setup (English/Arabic <math id="abstract1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> French), PTPP-aware formulations trained on early stages (<math id="abstract1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>={15,31}) predict target loss at <math id="abstract1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>=279 and outperform a PTPP-agnostic <span id="abstract1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">D</span><span id="abstract1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">-</span><span id="abstract1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">cpt</span> transfer baseline on metrics (Huber-on-log, MAE<sub id="abstract1.1.6" class="ltx_sub">rel</sub>, calibration slope); full diagnostics (RMSE, MAPE) are in the appendix. Beyond forecasting, we show a practical use case: planning replay ratios and adaptation token budgets that satisfy target and forgetting constraints under compute limits.</p>
  
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Capabilities of LLMs (large language models) continue to scale with model size, data size, and thus the total compute used for pre-training. Language models trained on a mixture of domains, dominated by web-scale corpora, yield general LLMs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Biderman et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dey et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">OLMo et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. These generalist models may not perform well in tasks requiring specialized knowledge (e.g., in fields such as medicine, law, finance) or those requiring language capabilities beyond the dominant pre-training language. We must therefore <em id="S1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">adapt</em> these models to new, domain-specific, or target-language-specific data.
This adaptation process presents a fundamental challenge: achieving strong performance in the target domain while preserving general capabilities (avoiding catastrophic forgetting <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kirkpatrick et al., 2017</a>)</cite>).
Various strategies have been proposed to minimize forgetting <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ostapenko et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Biderman et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ibrahim et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gupta et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Pre-training scaling laws are well established—e.g., relations between model/data size and performance in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kaplan et al. (2020)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hoffmann et al. (2022)</a></cite>—whereas CPT-specific laws are comparatively underexplored. D-CPT extends Chinchilla with <em id="S1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">replay</em> to study compute-optimal CPT at a fixed pre-training stage <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Que et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and forgetting laws quantify degradation on the pre-training domain at that stage <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bethune et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">However, most CPT scaling laws—D-CPT and forgetting laws included—assume a <em id="S1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">fixed</em> pre-training budget (a single <math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math> stage), which limits <em id="S1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">forecasting</em> across budgets. Prior work indicates that <math id="S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math> modulates learning dynamics and downstream adaptation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Springer et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ash and Adams, 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lyle et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kumar et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. We therefore condition explicitly on <math id="S1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding <em id="S1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">PTPP-aware</em> adaptation laws that predict target-domain loss at unseen <math id="S1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math> and clarify replay–stage interactions. Our central question: can a law fit at early stages (<math id="S1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>={15,31}) <em id="S1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">forecast</em> target validation loss at <math id="S1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>=279?</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Although our experiments focus on language adaptation, treating <math id="S1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math> as an explicit driver of adaptation dynamics is broadly applicable. Prior multilingual adaptation work underscores the need to mitigate and estimate forgetting while acquiring target competence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">de Vries and Nissim, 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fujii et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gosal et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Our contributions include:</p>
<ol id="S1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PTPP-aware adaptation laws.</span> We extend CPT scaling laws by integrating the pre-training budget (<math id="S1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>) as an explicit variable in the functional form.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forecasting at unseen <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> Fits at <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>=15,31 predict French loss at <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>=279 and outperform a <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>-agnostic <span id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">D</span><span id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">-</span><span id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">cpt</span> baseline on all metrics; a handful of 241M-scale “anchor” points at <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>=279 (20 calibration measurements at the evaluation stage) further improve accuracy at low-cost.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Planning under constraints.</span> Using the fitted law, we find an optimal replay ratio and adaptation token budget that satisfy target and forgetting constraints under compute limits.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Methodology and Experiments</h2>

<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h3>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We study loss <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{L}</annotation></semantics></math> as a function of model size <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, adaptation tokens <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, replay ratio <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\!\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\!\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> (s.t. <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-r</annotation></semantics></math> is the target domain fraction), and pre-training <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We use GPT-2–style decoder-only models pre-trained on a mixed English–Arabic corpus; the <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">adaptation domain</em> is French. Fits use <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>={15,31} and are <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">evaluated</em> on <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>=279 (unseen), across <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\{0.10,0.25,0.50\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\{0.10,0.25,0.50\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="N\in\{" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\in\{</annotation></semantics></math>241M, 517M, 1.4B, 8.1B<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>-Aware candidate formulations (1–3).</h3>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All laws share an <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>-term and an <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>-barrier; they differ in how <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math> affects the data-efficiency term. Let <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\!=\!10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\!=\!10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(1) Additive <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math> prior (floor).</h3>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{L}\;=\;E\;+\;\frac{A}{N^{\alpha}}\;+\;\frac{B\,r^{\nu}}{D^{\beta}}\;+\;\frac{C}{(r+\varepsilon_{r})^{\gamma}}\;+\;\frac{F}{\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\eta}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ν</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext><mi>η</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{L}\;=\;E\;+\;\frac{A}{N^{\alpha}}\;+\;\frac{B\,r^{\nu}}{D^{\beta}}\;+\;\frac{C}{(r+\varepsilon_{r})^{\gamma}}\;+\;\frac{F}{\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\eta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math> lowers the <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">floor</em> of <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{L}</annotation></semantics></math> via an additive term.</em></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(2) <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>gated data exponent (no floor).</h3>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{L}\;=\;E\;+\;\frac{A}{N^{\alpha}}\;+\;\frac{B\,r^{\nu}}{D^{\,\beta_{\!\text{eff}}}}\;+\;\frac{C}{(r+\varepsilon_{r})^{\gamma}},\qquad\beta_{\!\text{eff}}=\beta\!\left(1-\lambda\frac{\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\zeta}}{1+\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\zeta}}\right),\;\;\beta_{\!\text{eff}}\geq 10^{-6}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ν</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.448em;" width="0.448em"><mi>β</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext><mi>ζ</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext><mi>ζ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo>≥</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{L}\;=\;E\;+\;\frac{A}{N^{\alpha}}\;+\;\frac{B\,r^{\nu}}{D^{\,\beta_{\!\text{eff}}}}\;+\;\frac{C}{(r+\varepsilon_{r})^{\gamma}},\qquad\beta_{\!\text{eff}}=\beta\!\left(1-\lambda\frac{\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\zeta}}{1+\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\zeta}}\right),\;\;\beta_{\!\text{eff}}\geq 10^{-6}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math> controls the <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">shape</em> of the data law via a bounded gate <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\,\frac{\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\zeta}}{1+\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\zeta}}\in[0,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext><mi>ζ</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext><mi>ζ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\,\frac{\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\zeta}}{1+\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\zeta}}\in[0,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\!\text{eff}}=\beta\,(1-g(\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">eff</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\!\text{eff}}=\beta\,(1-g(\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}))</annotation></semantics></math>, representing the impact of pre-training budget on adaptation efficiency.</em></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(3) <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>gated data exponent <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">+</em> floor.</h3>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{L}\;=\;E\;+\;\frac{A}{N^{\alpha}}\;+\;\frac{B\,r^{\nu}}{D^{\,\beta_{\!\text{eff}}}}\;+\;\frac{C}{(r+\varepsilon_{r})^{\gamma}}\;+\;\frac{F}{\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\eta}},\qquad\beta_{\!\text{eff}}=\beta\!\left(1-\lambda\frac{\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\zeta}}{1+\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\zeta}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>L</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ν</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>γ</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext><mi>η</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mtext>eff</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.448em;" width="0.448em"><mi>β</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext><mi>ζ</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext><mi>ζ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{L}\;=\;E\;+\;\frac{A}{N^{\alpha}}\;+\;\frac{B\,r^{\nu}}{D^{\,\beta_{\!\text{eff}}}}\;+\;\frac{C}{(r+\varepsilon_{r})^{\gamma}}\;+\;\frac{F}{\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\eta}},\qquad\beta_{\!\text{eff}}=\beta\!\left(1-\lambda\frac{\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\zeta}}{1+\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\zeta}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math> acts <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">twice</em>: (i) a bounded gate reshapes the <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>-response (as in Form 2), and (ii) an additive prior <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F/\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext><mi>η</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F/\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}^{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> lowers the loss floor. This captures both shape and offset effects of pre-training.</em></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Anchors.</h3>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also report a few-shot variant that augments the fit with 20 small-scale (241M) <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">anchors</em> collected at the evaluation stage (<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>=279) across the <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r,D)</annotation></semantics></math> grid; all other <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>=279 points remain held out (unlike the oracle, which fits on the full <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>=279 set). These anchors tighten calibration (slope <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to 1</annotation></semantics></math>) and error metrics at low-cost.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data &amp; models.</h3>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GPT-2–style decoders are pre-trained on English/Arabic (source) and adapted to French (target). We consider <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math><math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\in\{15,31,279\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>279</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\in\{15,31,279\}</annotation></semantics></math>; replay <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\{0.10,0.25,0.50\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\{0.10,0.25,0.50\}</annotation></semantics></math>; and model sizes <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{</annotation></semantics></math>241M, 517M, 1.4B, 8.1B<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\}</annotation></semantics></math>. We focus on the French target; source-domain (English/Arabic) results are deferred to the appendix.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Fitting constraints.</h3>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We minimize Huber loss on log residuals (<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta{=}0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta{=}0.02</annotation></semantics></math>) with L–BFGS–B under positivity constraint for all parameters except <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. We clip <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\!\in[10^{-9},1-10^{-9}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\!\in[10^{-9},1-10^{-9}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Metrics.</h3>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assess predictions at <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>=279 with three metrics. <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Huber-on-log</em> is the Huber loss to residuals <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\log\hat{y}-\log y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\log\hat{y}-\log y</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0.02</annotation></semantics></math>. <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">MAE<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}_{\text{rel}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">rel</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}_{\text{rel}}</annotation></semantics></math></em> is the mean absolute relative error <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{1}{n}\!\sum_{i}\tfrac{|\hat{y}_{i}-y_{i}|}{y_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{n}\!\sum_{i}\tfrac{|\hat{y}_{i}-y_{i}|}{y_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., the typical percentage miss (lower is better). <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Calibration (intercept/slope)</em>: parameters <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math> from an Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) fit <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log y=a+b\,\log\hat{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log y=a+b\,\log\hat{y}</annotation></semantics></math>; ideal is <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px9.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\approx 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\approx 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Results: Forecasting at Unseen <math id="S3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<figure id="S3.T1" class="ltx_table">
