</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>French prediction at unseen <math id="S3.T1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>=279 (no anchors; trained on <math id="S3.T1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>={15,31}).
Full metrics (including calibration intercepts and RMSE) appear in Appendix <a href="#Ax1" title="Appendix A: Full metric tables ‣ PTPP-Aware Adaptation Scaling Laws:Predicting Domain-Adaptation Performance at Unseen Pre-Training Budgets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Appendix A: Full metric tables</span></a>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S3.F1" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.23198v1/d_cpt_scaling_law_fr.svg" id="S3.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/272;" width="476" height="272"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span><math id="S3.F1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>=279 <em id="S3.F1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">predictions</em> of the <em id="S3.F1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">gated+floor</em> model (dashed) vs. <em id="S3.F1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">observations</em> (markers) of validation loss for <math id="S3.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\{0.10,0.25,0.50\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\{0.10,0.25,0.50\}</annotation></semantics></math> and {241M, 517M, 1.4B, 8.1B}.</figcaption>
</figure>
