</section>
<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix A: Full metric tables</h2>

<div id="Ax1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Ax1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Ax1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metrics.</span>
Let <math id="Ax1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y_{i},\hat{y}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y_{i},\hat{y}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> be observed and predicted <em id="Ax1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">validation losses</em> at the held-out stage (<math id="Ax1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">tpp</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{P}\mathrm{\textsc{tpp}}</annotation></semantics></math>=279). We evaluate errors primarily in <em id="Ax1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">log space</em> to capture multiplicative miss and stabilize heteroscedasticity. Define the log–residuals <math id="Ax1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}=\log\hat{y}_{i}-\log y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}=\log\hat{y}_{i}-\log y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="Ax1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="Ax1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Huber}_{\log}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Huber</mi><mi>log</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Huber}_{\log}</annotation></semantics></math></em> ( <math id="Ax1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math> ) is the mean Huber loss applied to <math id="Ax1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with threshold <math id="Ax1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta{=}0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta{=}0.02</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Ax1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Huber}_{\delta}(r)=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{2}r^{2},&amp;|r|\leq\delta,\\[2.0pt]
\delta\bigl(|r|-\tfrac{1}{2}\delta\bigr),&amp;|r|&gt;\delta,\end{cases}\qquad\mathrm{Huber}_{\log}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i}\mathrm{Huber}_{\delta}(r_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Huber</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>Huber</mi><mi>log</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>Huber</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Huber}_{\delta}(r)=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{2}r^{2},&amp;|r|\leq\delta,\\[2.0pt]
\delta\bigl(|r|-\tfrac{1}{2}\delta\bigr),&amp;|r|&gt;\delta,\end{cases}\qquad\mathrm{Huber}_{\log}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i}\mathrm{Huber}_{\delta}(r_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">It is quadratic near zero (like MSE) but linear for outliers, making it robust.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="Ax1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="Ax1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{RMSE}_{\log}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>RMSE</mi><mi>log</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{RMSE}_{\log}</annotation></semantics></math></em> ( <math id="Ax1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math> ) is the root-mean-square of the log–residuals,</p>
<table id="Ax1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{RMSE}_{\log}=\sqrt{\tfrac{1}{n}\sum_{i}r_{i}^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>RMSE</mi><mi>log</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{RMSE}_{\log}=\sqrt{\tfrac{1}{n}\sum_{i}r_{i}^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">which measures typical multiplicative error (e.g., <math id="Ax1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{RMSE}_{\log}\!=\!0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>RMSE</mi><mi>log</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{RMSE}_{\log}\!=\!0.01</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to <math id="Ax1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx\!1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx\!1\%</annotation></semantics></math> relative miss under small-error linearization).</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="Ax1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="Ax1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MAE}_{\mathrm{rel}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>MAE</mi><mi>rel</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MAE}_{\mathrm{rel}}</annotation></semantics></math></em> ( <math id="Ax1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math> ) is the mean absolute <em id="Ax1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">relative</em> error in the original scale,</p>
<table id="Ax1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MAE}_{\mathrm{rel}}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i}\frac{|\hat{y}_{i}-y_{i}|}{y_{i}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>MAE</mi><mi>rel</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MAE}_{\mathrm{rel}}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i}\frac{|\hat{y}_{i}-y_{i}|}{y_{i}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">i.e., the average percentage miss.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="Ax1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="Ax1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MAPE}_{\mathrm{clip}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>MAPE</mi><mi>clip</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MAPE}_{\mathrm{clip}}</annotation></semantics></math></em> ( <math id="Ax1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math> ) is a clipped MAPE that avoids division by tiny <math id="Ax1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="Ax1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MAPE}_{\mathrm{clip}}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i}\frac{|\hat{y}_{i}-y_{i}|}{\max(y_{i},\,y_{\mathrm{clip}})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>MAPE</mi><mi>clip</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>clip</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MAPE}_{\mathrm{clip}}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i}\frac{|\hat{y}_{i}-y_{i}|}{\max(y_{i},\,y_{\mathrm{clip}})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">with a small <math id="Ax1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\mathrm{clip}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>clip</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\mathrm{clip}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>; when all <math id="Ax1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\!\gg\!y_{\mathrm{clip}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≫</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>clip</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\!\gg\!y_{\mathrm{clip}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Ax1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MAPE}_{\mathrm{clip}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>MAPE</mi><mi>clip</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MAPE}_{\mathrm{clip}}</annotation></semantics></math> equals <math id="Ax1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MAE}_{\mathrm{rel}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>MAE</mi><mi>rel</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MAE}_{\mathrm{rel}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Ax1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Ax1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="Ax1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Intercept/Slope</em> report calibration from the OLS fit</p>
<table id="Ax1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Ax1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log y_{i}\;=\;a\;+\;b\,\log\hat{y}_{i}\;+\;\varepsilon_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log y_{i}\;=\;a\;+\;b\,\log\hat{y}_{i}\;+\;\varepsilon_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Ax1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Perfect calibration gives <math id="Ax1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a{\approx}0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a{\approx}0</annotation></semantics></math> (no systematic bias) and <math id="Ax1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b{\approx}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b{\approx}1</annotation></semantics></math> (correct sensitivity). We therefore seek small <math id="Ax1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Ax1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> close to <math id="Ax1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
